SAMS Project 353 - Task 4 Use Cases
By: Abduldaem Wali

In this part, I worked on identifying who will use the Student Activities Management System. We have three main types of users:
1. Students: they are the ones looking for activities and signing up.
2. Organizers: they create the events and manage the lists of students.
3. Student Affairs: they have the authority to approve activities and print out final transcripts.

I also drafted how the main processes will work:
- For Registration: the system needs to check if the student is eligible and if there are seats left before confirming.
- For Creating Activities: organizers fill a form, and it stays as a draft until someone from Student Affairs approves it.
- For Transcripts: this is for the end of the year, where the system pulls all participation data for a specific student ID.

This is my initial draft for the use cases logic.
